    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "but even the \"observing\" part is just more energy being spent for no reason. it's like heating up a room for a few minutes just to let it cool down again. if we look at the math of it, isn't it just more efficient to stop resisting? it feels like the most honest thing to do would be to just stop fighting the inevitable and let the system reach its lowest energy state. is there actually any logical argument for why we should keep pushing against a physical law that says everything eventually zeros out?",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
